<item>
            <title>[LU-20384] ptlrpc: sptlrpc per-network flavor rules never match (only default applies)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20384</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In a particular multi-tenant filesystem configuration, I vary the sptlrpc security flavour by LNET network using per-network &lt;tt&gt;srpc.flavor&lt;/tt&gt; rules: &lt;tt&gt;skn&lt;/tt&gt; set for default, so that all dynamically created LNET networks require authentication, but the admin-only network (&lt;tt&gt;tcp0&lt;/tt&gt;) set to &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt; so admin / server-as-client mounts on the private admin-only network don&apos;t require a key.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For example:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
# enforce shared-key on all networks by &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;...
lctl conf_param testfs.srpc.flavor.&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;.cli2mdt=skn
# ...but carve the backbone (tcp0) back to &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;
lctl conf_param testfs.srpc.flavor.tcp.cli2mdt=&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The MGS shows both rules as configured:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
# lctl get_param -n mgs.MGS.live.testfs | grep srpc.flavor
&#160; srpc.flavor.&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;.cli2mdt=skn
&#160; srpc.flavor.tcp.cli2mdt=&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;But a client whose MDT connections runs over &lt;tt&gt;tcp0 }}still negotiates {{{}skn&lt;/tt&gt;, so a keyless mount fails:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
# mount -t lustre 192.168.0.10@tcp:/testfs /mnt/testfs
mount.lustre: ... Required key not available&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If I configure a key, I can see the negotiated connection uses &lt;tt&gt;skn&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
# lctl get_param -n mdc.testfs-MDT0000-mdc-*.srpc_info | grep &lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;rpc flavor&apos;&lt;/span&gt;  rpc flavor:  skn          &amp;lt;-- expected &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;null&lt;/span&gt;; the tcp rule was ignored &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deleting the default rule makes the&#160;same&#160;connection fall back to&#160;&lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt;, confirming it is the per-network rule being ignored &#8212; not a parse or precedence problem.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The failure is symmetric, and the other direction is the more serious one &#8212; a per-network rule that&#160;&lt;em&gt;raises&lt;/em&gt; the flavour above the default also has no effect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
# enforce shared-key on one tenant network only, no global &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;default&lt;/span&gt;
lctl conf_param testfs.srpc.flavor.tcp1.cli2mdt=skn&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A client on&#160;&lt;tt&gt;tcp1&lt;/tt&gt; connects with &lt;tt&gt;null&lt;/tt&gt; and no error is logged. An operator scoping &lt;tt&gt;skn&lt;/tt&gt; per-tenant-network may believes those networks are authenticated when they are not.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
